{
  "id": "flak",
  "options": [
    {
      "option": "F1",
      "label": "F1 · Ink-wash puff",
      "note": "PROPOSED. A flak burst is a dark soft cloud, built the way the soft white smoke is (stepped translucent washes, no outline, the map shows through) in the palette's ink instead of white, so it cannot be mistaken for damage smoke. A fast flash first: a ragged knock-out disc (the lightest step of the palette, no fire) with ink hatch rays and flung dots, a heavier flash and fragments on a hit. The cloud then hangs a few turns, lightening as it ages. Thick enough to cast a shadow by the altitude rule.",
      "rows": [
